  "question": {
    "text": "Let the equation of a line is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>. An insect starts flying from <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in a straight line meeting the given line at a point <math><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and then goes to the point <math><mi>Q</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in a straight line such that <math><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is perpendicular to <math><mi>R</mi><mi>Q.</mi></math>&nbsp;Then, the least value of <math><mn>7</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
